    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="31">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:LeisWl">Leis Wl</ref> 31</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-i"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#LeisWl_31.lnote.oe.8"/><pb n="513" ed="#liebermann"/>Si<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#LeisWl_31.lnote.oe.9"/> les seignurages ne facent altri gainurs<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#LeisWl_31.lnote.oe.10"/> venir a lour<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#LeisWl_31.lnote.oe.4"/> terre, la justise le facet.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-l"><pb n="513" ed="#liebermann"/>De terra colenda. Si domini terrarum non procurent<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="d" target="#LeisWl_31.lnote.oe.d"/> idoneos<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="e" target="#LeisWl_31.lnote.oe.e"/> cultores ad terras suas colendas<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="d" target="#LeisWl_31.lnote.oe.d"/>, iusticiarii<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="f" target="#LeisWl_31.lnote.oe.f"/> hoc faciant.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="xno" source="#robertson" n="31" corresp="#wit-i"><pb n="268" ed="#robertson"/>Si les seinurages ne facent altri gainurs venir a lour terre, la justise le facet.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="513" ed="#liebermann"/>31. Wenn die Grundherrschaften Landarbeiter eines anderen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#LeisWl_31.lnote.de.1"/> nicht auf deren Land [zurück]gehen lassen, soll der Richter [= Regierungsbeamte] dies bewirken.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">31. If the landlords do not let another's land-labourers go [back] to their land, the judge [= government official] shall bring this about.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-i"><pb n="269" ed="#robertson"/>If estate-owners do not make another man's workmen return to their estate, the court shall do so.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Added October 2026 from Robertson pp. 268–269 (text and translation); Liebermann’s text and German translation added from Gesetze I p. 513, October 2026 (two independent readings of the page images)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_31.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">513</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">lor <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lor Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_31.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">513</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">kein Absatz I</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">no paragraph break I</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_31.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">513</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">S les sein. <hi rend="italic">Im</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">S les sein. Im</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_31.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">513</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gainnys <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gainnys Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_31.lnote.oe.d" n="d" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">513</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">falsch</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">wrong</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_31.lnote.oe.e" n="e" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">513</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Römische Phraseologie</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Roman phraseology</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_31.lnote.oe.f" n="f" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">513</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">s. o.</hi> 22<hi rend="italic">a</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">see above</hi> 22<hi rend="italic">a</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="LeisWl_31.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">291</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">So richtig Kelham, Chevallet; missverstanden (wie Maitland <hi rend="italic">Domesday</hi> 51 erklärt) durch L (danach Schmid, Nasse) so, als ob der Staat sorge für Wiederansetzung der Bauern (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 10g) im Villanendorf. Zu L's Stil <hi rend="italic">vgl. coloni . . ut idoneiores praediis</hi> in l. 5 § 11 Dig. 50, 6.—<hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Königsrichter 3a. 11</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">So rightly Kelham, Chevallet; misunderstood (as Maitland <hi rend="italic">Domesday</hi> 51 explains) by L (and after him Schmid, Nasse) as if the state were seeing to the resettlement of the peasants (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 10g) in the villein township. On L’s style <hi rend="italic">cf. coloni . . ut idoneiores praediis</hi> in l. 5 § 11 Dig. 50, 6.—<hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Königsrichter 3a. 11</seg></note>
      </div>
